(A) R1 exhaustively: every data law is shared by C(2^m, s0) worlds with pairwise different humans
  m = 3, s0 = 1: 2048 worlds, 256 data laws (all 2^8 tables T: True); worlds per data law = {8}; humans distinct within each law: True; best average success = 0.125000 = 1/8 = 1/C(8,1) = 0.125000
  m = 3, s0 = 2: 7168 worlds, 256 data laws (all 2^8 tables T: True); worlds per data law = {28}; humans distinct within each law: True; best average success = 0.035714 = 1/28 = 1/C(8,2) = 0.035714
  m = 3, s0 = 3: 14336 worlds, 256 data laws (all 2^8 tables T: True); worlds per data law = {56}; humans distinct within each law: True; best average success = 0.017857 = 1/56 = 1/C(8,3) = 0.017857
  m = 4, s0 = 2: 7864320 worlds, 65536 data laws (all 2^16 tables T: True); worlds per data law = {120}; humans distinct within each law: True; best average success = 0.008333 = 1/120 = 1/C(16,2) = 0.008333

